               ],
               note: "The no-stirring rule is absolute. Stirring releases starch and makes risotto; paella rice must sit still, drink the broth, and toast against the pan floor.",
               shortcut: "All chicken, no rabbit, changes little for a US kitchen. Skipping bomba rice for long-grain, though, costs you the whole texture; use any short-grain first."),
        Recipe(dishID: "spain-gazpacho", serves: 4, prepMinutes: 20, cookMinutes: 0, difficulty: 1,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 lb", item: "ripe tomatoes, cored and chopped"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2", item: "cucumber, peeled"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1", item: "green bell pepper, seeded"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 slices", item: "day-old white bread, crusts removed"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 clove", item: "garlic"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 tbsp", item: "sherry vinegar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "olive oil"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "cold water"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Tear the bread into a bowl with the chopped tomatoes and let it soak in their juice for 10 minutes while you prep everything else. The bread is the ancient thickener here.",
                   "Blend the soaked bread and tomatoes with the cucumber, green pepper, garlic, vinegar, salt, and cold water on high until completely smooth, a full 2 minutes.",
                   "With the blender running, stream in the olive oil slowly. The soup will lighten from red to a pale salmon-orange and turn noticeably creamy; that is the emulsion you want.",
                   "Push the soup through a fine sieve, pressing with a ladle, and discard the skins and seeds. This step separates gazpacho from salsa; do not skip it.",
                   "Chill at least 2 hours, until properly cold. Taste after chilling and correct the salt and vinegar; cold blunts both, so it will need more than you think.",
                   "Serve in glasses to drink or bowls with a thread of olive oil, and pass small dishes of diced cucumber, pepper, and onion for topping.",
               ],
